⏺ I've got a clear picture of the structure. Before finalizing, two things need clarification — the collapsibility request, and the heading font.

  ★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
  - Hooks emit a systemMessage over stderr as plain ANSI text. Claude Code's TUI doesn't expose interactive click handlers to hook output — the "jump to bottom" button in your screenshot is a
  built-in TUI affordance, not something a hook can render. So true click-to-collapse isn't possible from this side.
  - The current bind.mjs is a flat switch of handlers + ad-hoc rendering in each one. A Renderer class with per-tool strategies (registry pattern) cleanly splits "what to extract" from "how to
  render".
  - The PAGGA glyph table at utils.mjs:647-676 is the heading. Several letters (J, K, S, Y) use inconsistent strokes vs. their neighbors — that's the "off" rendering you see.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

